---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const site = 'https://www.ewohub.com';
const slug = 'chaturbate-tip-menu';
---

<Base
  title="Chaturbate Tip Menu: How to Build One That Earns"
  description="How to build a Chaturbate tip menu that gets used: pricing ladders, token math, tip menu vs goals, common mistakes and how to test and adjust prices based on what viewers actually tip."
  lang="en"
  hreflang={[{ lang: 'en', url: `${site}/${slug}` }]}
  articleMeta={{ datePublished: '2026-09-24' }}
>

  <section class="art-hero">
    <div class="art-orb art-orb--1"></div>
    <div class="art-orb art-orb--2"></div>
    <div class="art-grid"></div>
    <div class="art-hero__inner container">
      <div class="art-meta">
        <span class="art-tag">Chaturbate</span>
        <span class="art-tag art-tag--green">How-to</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="art-title">Chaturbate Tip Menu: <span class="art-grad">Build One That Earns</span></h1>
      <p class="art-lead">
        A tip menu turns "how do I tip?" into an obvious next step. Set up well, it raises the number of tips per hour,
        which is what keeps a room moving up the listings. Here is how to price it, structure it and improve it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="art-body container">
    <div class="art-layout">
      <aside class="art-toc">
        <p class="art-toc__title">Contents</p>
        <ol class="art-toc__list">
          <li><a href="#what">What a tip menu is</a></li>
          <li><a href="#why">Why it matters</a></li>
          <li><a href="#math">Token math</a></li>
          <li><a href="#ladder">Building a price ladder</a></li>
          <li><a href="#menu-vs-goals">Tip menu vs goals</a></li>
          <li><a href="#mistakes">Common mistakes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
        <a href="#cta" class="art-toc__cta">Get help →</a>
      </aside>

      <main class="art-main">

        <p class="art-intro">
          On Chaturbate, a tip menu is the list of actions viewers can trigger by tipping a specific number of
          tokens. It gives every viewer a clear, low-effort way to participate. The examples below are starting points
          to test, not fixed rules — your audience decides what works.
        </p>
        <p class="card-date" style="margin:0 0 1.75rem;">EWOhub Editorial Team · Published Sep 24, 2026</p>

        <section class="section" id="what">
          <h2>What a Tip Menu Is</h2>
          <div class="glass-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <p>
              A tip menu lists what viewers get for a given tip amount. It lives in your room settings and is shown to
              anyone who enters. Unlike a goal, which is one target with a single payoff, a menu offers several small
              options at once, so more viewers have something they can afford.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
              Room rules and features change, so check Chaturbate's current settings and terms before you set yours up.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="why">
          <h2>Why It Matters for Ranking and Income</h2>
          <div class="glass-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <p>
              Discovery on Chaturbate rewards active rooms, and tip frequency is a strong engagement signal. A clear
              menu produces more small tips, which lifts income directly and helps visibility indirectly — the mechanics
              are in <a href="/how-cam-algorithm-ranks-rooms">how cam algorithms rank rooms</a>.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
              It also removes friction. Viewers who do not know what a tip does are less likely to tip at all.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="math">
          <h2>Token Math</h2>
          <div class="glass-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <p>
              Standard Chaturbate broadcasters are paid a flat $0.05 per token, so a 100-token tip is worth $5 to you
              before any studio share or taxes. Price every item against that number, not the price the viewer sees, so
              you know what each request is worth in real money. The <a href="/stripchat-chaturbate-token-calculator">token
              calculator</a> does the conversion for you.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
              For more on how the platform pays, see <a href="/webcam-earnings-by-platform">webcam earnings by platform</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="ladder">
          <h2>Building a Price Ladder</h2>
          <p>Aim for a spread of price points so that every viewer has something within reach:</p>
          <div class="reason-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <div class="reason-num">01</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Entry level</h3>
              <p>Low-token, quick actions that anyone can afford. These create the habit of tipping and drive frequency.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">02</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Mid level</h3>
              <p>Actions worth a noticeable tip. Most of your income tends to come from here once the room warms up.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">03</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Premium level</h3>
              <p>A few high-token items for your biggest supporters. Keep the list short so it stays special.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="menu-vs-goals">
          <h2>Tip Menu vs Goals</h2>
          <div class="two-col-box">
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--good">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">TIP MENU</p>
              <p>Many small options, always available. Best for steady tip frequency and for viewers who tip alone.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--bad">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">GOAL</p>
              <p>One shared target that the room fills together. Best for building momentum and group participation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            Use both. The structure principles are covered in <a href="/stripchat-goals-tip-menu-structure">goals and
            tip menu structure</a>, and your room title and tags do the work of bringing people in — see
            <a href="/top-performing-titles-chaturbate">top-performing titles</a> and
            <a href="/top-performing-tags-chaturbate">top-performing tags</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="mistakes">
          <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
          <div class="checklist">
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Too many items.</strong> A long list is hard to read, so viewers skip it.</li>
              <li><strong>Only expensive options.</strong> If nothing is affordable, most viewers will not tip.</li>
              <li><strong>Never updating it.</strong> Review it weekly against what viewers actually tip.</li>
              <li><strong>Pricing from the viewer's side.</strong> Convert to your payout so you know what your time is worth.</li>
              <li><strong>Ignoring the room's rules.</strong> Keep every item within the platform's current terms.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="faq-section section" id="faq">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How many items should a tip menu have?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Keep it short enough to read at a glance. A small set across entry, mid and premium price points usually works better than a long list. Test and remove items nobody uses.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How much is a Chaturbate token worth?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Standard broadcasters get a flat $0.05 per token; Fan Club members can earn $0.06–$0.08. Confirm your own rate in the dashboard.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Should I use a tip menu and goals together?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. The menu keeps individual tipping steady, while a goal gives the room a shared target to rally around.</p></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cta" class="art-cta section">
          <div class="art-cta__orb"></div>
          <div class="art-cta__inner">
            <span class="art-cta__badge">Need viewers to tip?</span>
            <h2>A good menu needs an audience</h2>
            <p>We bring viewers into Chaturbate rooms so your tip menu has people to work on. Tell us your platform and goals.</p>
            <div class="art-cta__actions">
              <a href="https://t.me/+tBjfmjh9vHo1YzQy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="art-cta__btn art-cta__btn--primary">Talk to us →</a>
              <a href="/model-promotion" class="art-cta__btn art-cta__btn--ghost">Promotion services</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>Related Articles</h2>
          <div class="related-grid">
            <a href="/chaturbate-show-prices" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🏷️</span>
              <span>Chaturbate Show Prices</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/stripchat-goals-tip-menu-structure" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🎯</span>
              <span>Goals and Tip Menu Structure</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/top-performing-tags-chaturbate" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🏷</span>
              <span>Top-Performing Tags on Chaturbate</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/top-performing-titles-chaturbate" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">✍️</span>
              <span>Top-Performing Titles on Chaturbate</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/stripchat-chaturbate-token-calculator" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🧰</span>
              <span>Token Calculator</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/how-cam-algorithm-ranks-rooms" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">📈</span>
              <span>How Cam Algorithms Rank Rooms</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </main>
    </div>
  </div>

</Base>
